From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:04:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mask the text of password fields

An `<input type="password">` laid out and drew its value. Its editor now
holds one U+2022 BULLET per character of the value, which the field keeps
beside it (`TextInputData::secret`), so the value is never laid out,
drawn, selected or measured: caret and selection positions don't give
away the widths of its characters.

An edit is masked after it runs (`unmask_edit`, from the `input` event):
an edit replaces a range with new text and leaves the caret after it, so
the unmasked characters before the caret are the new text and the masks
either side are what is left of the value. A preedit is masked once it's
committed. The `input` event and form submission read the value
(`TextInputData::value`), and setting `value` masks it. A field that
becomes a password, or stops being one, when it's laid out again is
masked or shown.
---
